9e5","position":"1787343161480447001-6f9978aa-6b2d-4da5-84f3-e3757eeb506f"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"7ce895fe57add9156b1f05cf4e3ef579fb5098915c3a1c62c36556bb713ffc21","event_uuid":"802d7f8d-da28-49b6-8ee8-60fa1ba04ca7","position":{"commit_sha":"d2b73f7d37cb0274cdcc9178859a19935bf6137d","position":"1787343729389194605-802d7f8d-da28-49b6-8ee8-60fa1ba04ca7"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"close_class":"plan_defect","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implementation complete in worktree fix-3ff9; RED->GREEN per plan.\n\nRED: tests/unit/test_push_expected_contention_quiet.py failed 5/7 on unfixed code for the pinned reasons (WARNING at push.py:323 terminal-after-recovery with raw \"! [rejected]\" stderr and the \"..HEAD\" suffix; recovery-leg transport notices at WARNING; backlog_grew absent; strict message pinned old wording).\n\nGREEN (all changes logging/wording only - no behavior, classification, retry, or marker change):\n- push_state.unpushed_summary now reads \"(N unpushed commits on the local tickets branch ahead of origin/tickets; committed locally, they publish on the next successful push)\" - names the branch, no bare ..HEAD, self-healing contract in-text.\n- push_state.backlog_grew reads the PREVIOUS marker's unpushed count (state the marker already stored) before record_failure overwrites it; ambiguity resolves to False.\n- push_classify._terminal_severity: WARNING only for a policy decline in the terminal stderr or a PROVEN-growing backlog (suffix gains \"the backlog GREW since the previous failure\"); otherwise INFO with \"expected under concurrent tickets writers - no action needed\".\n- push.py: both terminal contention sites (retry-exhausted \"failed after N retries\" and \"terminal push failed after recovery\") now logger.log at that severity; both pinned literals appended-to, never reworded - epoch-guard negative assertions honored, not retargeted.\n- Mid-retry transient-transport notices demoted to INFO at all three sites (push_classify._retry_transport_or_stop, push_recovery fetch-leg and merge-leg), wording \"retrying automatically, no action needed\".\n- Consciously retargeted pins in the same change: test_push_strict.py (capture at INFO + level assertion), test_push_strict_happy.py and test_push_rejection_surfacing.py (new summary wording).\n\nVerification: new suite 7/7; targeted push/epoch-guard selection 107 passed with ONE failure - test_inline_write_push::test_a_write_pushing_to_the_origin_leaves_no_detached_upkeep - proven PRE-EXISTING: reproduced 2/2 on unmodified origin/main (a1a6a151bc) with baseline sources, passes alone and in all probed pairs. Filed as hypodermal-cacotopic-zenaida (d720-fc72-3763-4cac), linked discovered_from. make lint PASS; make typecheck PASS; complexity ratchet: new=0 increased=0 stale=1 (a function got simpler - sanctioned, baseline untouched).\n\nNext: commit with rebar-ticket trailer + DCO, push gerrit HEAD:refs/for/main, wait LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1, Submit, then close.","timestamp":1787338427684568001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Landed: Gerrit change 2017 (https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/2017), merged as 8c71e91a54 with LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1 (CI run 32515800055, SUCCESS). One non-blocking advisory from the reviewer (policy-decline branch of _terminal_severity lacks a direct unit test — it is exercised indirectly via the rejection-surfacing suite). Closed as plan_defect: the original 2a76 escalation surfaced expected/self-healing contention outcomes at WARNING.","timestamp":1787341635091809001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Operator ruling update (2026-08-21, verbatim, attributed to the operator): \"We should suppress the message under normal load. This is noise, not an outage signal.\"\n\nInterpretation recorded with the ruling: under normal load — ordinary contention losses, transient transport retries, and the routine unpushed-backlog suffix — these messages must be SUPPRESSED from agent-visible output entirely (DEBUG at most), not merely reworded at WARNING/INFO. A merely non-zero or shared backlog count is NOT an outage signal. WARNING remains reserved for genuine operator-actionable outage signals only: policy declines, strict-mode failures, and persistent failure clearly beyond normal concurrent-writer contention. The durable marker / fsck PUSH_PENDING observability stays as-is. Reopening to strengthen the ACs and demote the expected-case emissions from INFO to DEBUG.","timestamp":1787341712834542001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Ruling-update implementation pushed: Gerrit change 2021 (https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/2021), commit 1eb83440b7. RED->GREEN: retargeted the quiet suite (expected case now asserts NOTHING at INFO or above; recovery-leg notices DEBUG) and test_push_strict (mid-retry pin -> DEBUG); 4 intended RED failures, then demoted the four emission sites (push_classify mid-retry + _terminal_severity expected branch, push_recovery merge/fetch legs) from INFO to DEBUG. Loud cases untouched: policy decline WARNING, strict raise, proven-growing backlog WARNING. Gates: targeted 130 tests pass, make lint PASS, make typecheck PASS, complexity ratchet new=0 increased=0 stale=1. Waiting on LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1.","timestamp":1787343161480447001}],"created_at":1787335311461164001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"3f229833-4625-4288-afd3-56bb79744ec3","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"7558-f07e-551f-4593"},{"link_uuid":"802d7f8d-da28-49b6-8ee8-60fa1ba04ca7","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"0040-f7d8-2c03-450e"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nBest-effort tickets-branch push failures that are EXPECTED and AUTO-HANDLED are surfaced to\nagent-visible stderr at WARNING with wording that primes LLM agent sessions to assume the\nstore is broken. Two 2026-08-21 session reports (~12 concurrent writers) show agents halting\nwork to inspect `push.py` for a state that heals on the next successful write. Operator ruling\n(2026-08-21): \"If these issues are expected and handled automatically, we need to stop\nsurfacing them to sessions because it primes them to assume there's an issue and burn tokens\ninvestigating.\" Ruling update (2026-08-21): \"We should suppress the message under normal load.\nThis is noise, not an outage signal.\" — so under normal load (ordinary contention losses,\ntransient transport retries, the routine unpushed-backlog suffix) the messages are suppressed\nfrom agent-visible output entirely (DEBUG at most), and a merely non-zero or shared backlog\ncount is NOT an outage signal.\n\n## Offending messages (all logger.warning, agent-visible)\n\n1. `push.py:342` — \"tickets branch push failed after 3 retries: <raw git stderr><suffix>\" after\n   losing a CONTENTION race; raw git stderr pattern-matches corruption to an LLM (`unable to\n   update local ref`, `! [rejected]`). The sibling terminal site `push.py:323` \"terminal push\n   failed after recovery\" is the same lost-contention outcome, same treatment.\n2. `push_classify.py:225` — \"transient transport fault (attempt x/y), retrying\" — the code is\n   already retrying itself; pure worry-bait.\n3. `push_state.py:148` `unpushed_summary` — the \"(N unpushed commits on origin/tickets..HEAD)\"\n   suffix: \"HEAD\" is the TRACKER's HEAD but a session reads it as its code worktree HEAD; the\n   count escalates across ALL concurrent sessions; nothing states the self-healing contract.\n\n## What must STAY loud (bug 2a76's rationale is still valid)\n\n- Policy declines (hook declined, GH013, branch protection) — permanent, operator-actionable.\n- Strict-mode callers — PushDeliveryError already raises; unchanged.\n- A PERSISTENT/GROWING backlog — fsck PUSH_PENDING and the durable rebar-push-pending marker\n  are the operator channels; a terminal failure with a PROVEN-growing count stays WARNING.\n\n## Approach\n\nLogging/wording only — no change to push behavior, classification, retries, or the durable\nmarker. The first landing (Gerrit 2017, 8c71e91a54) did steps 1–2 and demoted the expected\npaths to INFO; the ruling update reopens this to demote them further, INFO → DEBUG (steps\n3–5 as now worded). Encode expected-and-self-healing vs operator-actionable at the reporting\nseam (`push_classify`):\n\n1. (LANDED in 2017) `push_state.unpushed_summary` names the tickets branch explicitly (no\n   bare `..HEAD`) and states the self-healing contract: committed locally, publish on the\n   next successful push. The suffix stays factual for policy declines — the \"no action\n   needed\" clause is appended only on the demoted path (pt 3).\n2. (LANDED in 2017) `push_state.backlog_grew(tracker, remote_ref)` — read-only compare of\n   the current `unpushed_count` against the previous push-pending marker's `unpushed` count\n   (no new persistent state). Ambiguity resolves to False — growth must be PROVEN before a\n   report escalates to operator-loud.\n3. `_terminal_severity` in `push_classify` (landed in 2017) returns (log level, backlog\n   suffix) for a terminal best-effort push failure: WARNING for a policy decline in the\n   terminal stderr or a proven-growing backlog stays; THIS change lowers the otherwise branch\n   from INFO to DEBUG, keeping the appended \"expected under concurrent tickets writers — no\n   action needed\" clause. Still called BEFORE `_raise_if_strict` records the new marker.\n4. The two terminal lost-contention sites in `push.py` already log via\n   `logger.log(level, ...)` from that helper (landed in 2017) — no push.py change needed; the\n   pinned literals \"failed after %s retries\" / \"terminal push failed after recovery\" and the\n   epoch-guard negative assertions stay honored.\n5. Demote every mid-retry transient-transport notice from INFO (post-2017) to DEBUG, keeping\n   the \"retrying automatically, no action needed\" wording: `_retry_transport_or_stop` in\n   `push_classify` plus the recovery-leg notices in `push_recovery.py` (merge-leg, fetch-leg).\n   The TERMINAL transport/policy warnings stay WARNING (bug 2a76 / f61c rationale).\n\nTests pinning the post-2017 level are retargeted in the same change: `test_push_strict.py`\n(mid-retry capture level) and the quiet-suite level assertions.\n\n## Scope\n\n- src/rebar/_store/push_classify.py — mid-retry demotion to DEBUG; terminal-severity helper\n  returns DEBUG for the expected case (was INFO after the first landing).\n- src/rebar/_store/push_recovery.py — demote the merge-leg and fetch-leg mid-retry\n  transient-transport notices to DEBUG (same class, same wording contract).\n- tests/unit/test_push_expected_contention_quiet.py — retarget: expected-case silence at INFO\n  and above + worry-free wording + growing-backlog escalation + no bare `..HEAD`.\n- tests/unit/test_push_strict.py — retarget the mid-retry level pin to DEBUG.\n- push.py / push_state.py / test_push_strict_happy.py / test_push_rejection_surfacing.py —\n  unchanged this round (their 2017 state already satisfies the ACs).\n\n## Testing\n\nRED→GREEN (the retargeted tests fail on current main, pass after the fix), all caplog-level\nassertions on the `rebar._store` loggers:\n\n- Expected case: a retry-exhausted lost contention race (every push non-fast-forward-rejected,\n  recovery merges clean, no prior marker) emits NO record at INFO or above; a DEBUG record\n  carries \"failed after N retries\", names the tickets branch, and states \"expected under\n  concurrent\" + \"no action needed\"; no message contains bare `..HEAD`.\n- Mid-retry transient transport notice is captured at DEBUG, below INFO.\n- Growing backlog: with a prior marker recording a smaller `unpushed` count, the same terminal\n  contention failure logs at WARNING (the sanctioned escalation).\n- Preserved loud cases: the existing real-git policy-decline suite\n  (test_push_rejection_surfacing) still passes at WARNING with reason + backlog count; strict\n  callers still raise PushDeliveryError (test_push_strict / test_push_strict_happy).\n\nVerification: targeted pytest on the push/epoch-guard suites (tests/unit/test_push_*.py,\ntest_epoch_guard_matrix.py, tests/integration/test_epoch_guard_reconciliation.py,\ntests/unit/test_commit_and_push*, tests/interfaces/store/test_fsck_push_pending.py), then\n`make lint` and `make typecheck`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A lost contention race on a best-effort write emits NOTHING at INFO or above (DEBUG at\n      most), while the state remains observable via push_status()/fsck PUSH_PENDING/marker.\n      Checked by the new caplog test (no records >= INFO) plus the marker/fsck suites green.\n- [ ] Mid-retry transient transport messages (push_classify + both push_recovery legs) are\n      DEBUG or below. Checked by caplog levels in test_push_strict.py and the new suite.\n- [ ] Every remaining backlog message names the tickets branch explicitly (no bare `..HEAD`),\n      with the self-healing contract stated in the message text. Checked by wording assertions\n      on the emitted records and the strict-message pins.\n- [ ] Policy declines, strict failures, and a proven-GROWING backlog remain WARNING/raise,\n      byte-compatible where tests pin them (reason token, GH013 passthrough, backlog count).\n      Checked by test_push_rejection_surfacing and test_push_strict staying green.\n- [ ] Tests pin expected-case silence at INFO and above, worry-free wording, plus the\n      preserved loud cases. Checked RED on current main, GREEN after the fix.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_store/push_classify.py","reason":"mid-retry and terminal expected-case demotion to DEBUG"},{"path":"src/rebar/_store/push_recovery.py","reason":"recovery-leg transport notices to DEBUG"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_push_expected_contention_quiet.py","reason":"retarget silence threshold to INFO-and-above"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_push_strict.py","reason":"retarget mid-retry level pin to DEBUG"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_reopened_at":1787341741273269001,"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","0040-f7d8-2c03-450e"],["relates_to","7558-f07e-551f-4593"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"c973199d-0aea-41da-922f-f5684507d3ce","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"3ff9-a8f0-ff5a-457f","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Expected tickets-push contention warnings prime agent sessions to investigate non-issues","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["3f229833-4625-4288-afd3-56bb79744ec3","ee348a43-1478-4b41-957d-aa9ccc97f98d","d3aa4485-2367-4dce-93d7-ae5fac358541","9b27eef0-e5b5-4dd9-b7e2-2cf4ab381b21","48de002b-fe37-4c9d-8afd-3a69cf06debf","ce562ada-2379-41cf-84ba-3a881b0d4cb8","7dcb87cd-1ab7-4e14-b8c4-5d0575e7ad04","d6395f1f-8380-4b4b-b4b5-977327c3ef66","87ec56d1-6cc7-4ccc-b411-46aeb4757b80","a058342e-cc62-49fc-81b0-38c1d06dff6d","c7ed7750-14c8-495b-bc67-6b04a624dbcf","8231d161-c0a1-4d15-9bf3-acea9e553986","c973199d-0aea-41da-922f-f5684507d3ce","81fa7ec1-1914-4632-b363-7a04786aca77","6f9978aa-6b2d-4da5-84f3-e3757eeb506f","802d7f8d-da28-49b6-8ee8-60fa1ba04ca7"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787346203642756001,"uuid":"a17ff996-7ce5-42c7-95d6-d3d9c4ec356e"}